    - target: {fileID: 1990594193549166204, guid: 1a2dbbbdb56be6943bcfd67626dc1ff6, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "A small percentage of people, when exposed to flashing lights or specific
        visual patterns, may experience epileptic seizures. Certain backgrounds or
        effects on screens, including those in video games, can trigger seizures
        in these individuals.  Even without a history of epilepsy, some may experience
        unexpected symptoms under these conditions. \n\nIf you notice dizziness,
        altered vision, muscle twitches, loss of awareness, disorientation, involuntary
        movements, or convulsions while using a computer or video game, STOP PLAYING
        IMMEDIATELY and consult your doctor before continuing."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 1990594193549166204, guid: 1a2dbbbdb56be6943bcfd67626dc1ff6, type: 3}
